From: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 11:59:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 15/15] fix: validate encoder changes before invoking control
 helpers

Reject unsupported metadata and coding changes, validate token and scalar limits, and preserve live settings when optional fields are omitted.

Fixes: 135cec8b6b04 ("feat: delegate encoder configuration to external helpers")
Signed-off-by: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
---
 CONTROL_HELPERS.md     |   3 +
 README.md              |   7 ++
 conf.c                 |  10 ++-
 control_helper.c       |   4 +-
 device_advertisement.c |  27 +++++---
 encoder_control.c      | 148 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-----
 media_profiles.c       |   3 +-
 onvif_simple_server.h  |   1 +
 test/test_cgi.py       |  32 +++++++++
 9 files changed, 207 insertions(+), 28 deletions(-)

--- a/CONTROL_HELPERS.md
+++ b/CONTROL_HELPERS.md
@@ -56,6 +56,9 @@ effective `configuration` after applying
 true, as required by the current Media specification; Media2 also persists
 encoder changes. Rejected changes must leave the camera unchanged. Setters
 remain unavailable when no encoder helper is configured.
+Omitted optional rate-control and GOP/profile members retain live values.
+Name, use count, multicast and session metadata remain read-only. Requests
+to change these or unsupported coding features return a fault.
 
 ## Imaging operations
 
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -396,6 +396,13 @@ Usage: /tmp/sd/yi-hack/bin/onvif_notify_
 | debug | debug level from 0 to 5 | 0 |
 
 ## Compatibility
+Profile names derive encoder tokens by appending `_VideoEncoderToken`.
+Keep names within 46 UTF-8 bytes so the generated token fits ONVIF's
+64-character ReferenceToken limit. H265 profiles use `Main` or `Main10`.
+Optional camera controls and their generic helper protocol are described in
+[CONTROL_HELPERS.md](CONTROL_HELPERS.md). Host protocol tests are described in
+[test/README.md](test/README.md).
+
 I tested this program with the following clients:
 - Onvif Device Manager (Windows)
 - Synology Surveillance Station (DSM 6.x and 7.x)
